{"timestamp":"2026-05-08T08:33:48.810Z","type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"agent_message","message":"`test:integration` is quiet because it is one big Go package.\n\nIn [mise.toml](/Users/alex/workspace/cli/.worktrees/1/mise.toml:18), it runs:\n\n```sh\ngo test -tags=integration ./cmd/entire/cli/integration_test/...\n```\n\nThat package has a `TestMain` that first builds a real `entire` binary before tests run: [setup_test.go](/Users/alex/workspace/cli/.worktrees/1/cmd/entire/cli/integration_test/setup_test.go:13). Then most tests create temp git repos and invoke that binary as a subprocess through `execx.NonInteractive`: [testenv.go](/Users/alex/workspace/cli/.worktrees/1/cmd/entire/cli/integration_test/testenv.go:148).\n\nSo the runtime is real integration work: binary build, temp repos, git commits, hooks, remotes, rewinds, session metadata, subprocess startup.\n\nWhy no output: raw `go test` without `-v` prints package output only when the package finishes or fails. `gotestsum --format pkgname` has the same issue here because there is only one package, so there are no intermediate package lines to print.\n\nI ran it with per-test output:\n\n```sh\ngotestsum --format testname --format-icons text --hide-summary skipped -- -tags=integration ./cmd/entire/cli/integration_test/...\n```\n\nThat produced steady progress and finished `324` tests in about `88s`, with one local failure:\n\n```text\nTestLogin_SavesTokenAfterApproval\nlogin_test.go:91: login command failed: exit status 1\nOutput:\nWaiting for approval...\nsave auth token: save token to keyring: exit status 161\n```\n\nThat failure is from the login integration test saving to the real local keyring: [login_test.go](/Users/alex/workspace/cli/.worktrees/1/cmd/entire/cli/integration_test/login_test.go:89). The subprocess env does not inject a mock keyring backend: [login_test.go](/Users/alex/workspace/cli/.worktrees/1/cmd/entire/cli/integration_test/login_test.go:193).\n\nThe slowest tests are mostly real checkpoint/session flows. Top examples from the run:\n\n```text\nTestShadow_MultipleCommits_SameActiveTurn            22.34s\nTestSubagentAccumulation_Issue591                    20.38s\nTestMultipleReadOnlySessions_NoneCondensed           19.8s\nTestHookOverwrite_MidTurnWipe_NextPromptRecovers     19.41s\nTestReadOnlySession_ActiveAcrossMultipleCommits      19.35s\n```\n\nSo: it is not hung; it is quiet because of package-level output, and slow because it is doing real CLI/git integration work. The better `mise` command for this task should probably use `gotestsum --format testname`, not `pkgname`.","phase":"final_answer","memory_citation":null}}
