{"timestamp":"2026-05-08T11:03:12.639Z","type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"mcp_tool_call_end","call_id":"call_kAL0B09We6ngl3sm1Xk9Ohmy","invocation":{"server":"codex_apps","tool":"linear_get_issue","arguments":{"id":"ENT-488","includeRelations":true,"includeCustomerNeeds":false}},"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":931809833},"result":{"Ok":{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"{\"id\":\"ENT-488\",\"title\":\"Speed up integration CI by skipping gnome-keyring install\",\"description\":\"## Context\\n\\nThe `integration` job in `.github/workflows/ci-integration.yml` currently spends \\\\~4 minutes on `apt-get update && apt-get install -y gnome-keyring dbus-x11` and related daemon setup. That's roughly half of the \\\\~9m30s job.\\n\\nTiming from run 24544052559 (temp/2 PR #843):\\n\\n| Phase | Duration |\\n| -- | -- |\\n| Setup Keyring and Identity | 4m25s |\\n| Run integration tests | 4m36s |\\n| Everything else | \\\\~30s |\\n\\nWithin the test step, `go: downloading` + compile is \\\\~10s — deps are not the problem.\\n\\n## Why the keyring is there\\n\\nThe integration tests exercise the CLI auth flow, which stores OAuth tokens via the `tokenstore` package. Its default backend delegates to the OS keyring via `github.com/zalando/go-keyring`, which on Linux talks to the Secret Service over dbus — hence the gnome-keyring install.\\n\\nOn user workstations the CLI does use the OS keyring (macOS Keychain / Linux Secret Service / Windows Credential Manager). Server nodes don't import `tokenstore` at all, so this is purely a CLI + CI concern.\\n\\n## The fix already exists\\n\\nPR #457 (`89230ae1`) added a file-backed `tokenstore` backend **explicitly for CI environments without a system keyring**, gated by `ENTIRE_TOKEN_STORE=file`. `.github/workflows/perf-nightly.yml` uses it. `ci-integration.yml` was never updated.\\n\\nProposed change: set `ENTIRE_TOKEN_STORE: file` in the integration job's `env:` block and delete the gnome-keyring install step. Expected saving: \\\\~4 minutes per run.\\n\\n## Follow-ups (separate tickets)\\n\\n* `entireio/cli` also installs gnome-keyring in its CI (Stefan copied the pattern from entiredb in Mar 2026). Could adopt the same file-backed approach there.\\n* `entire.io/test` package runs as a single 2m42s serial block — splitting into subpackages or using `t.Parallel()` would shave further time.\\n* `test:simulation` runs sequentially after integration tests in the same shell task; could be a parallel GHA job.\",\"priority\":{\"value\":3,\"name\":\"Medium\"},\"url\":\"https://linear.app/entirehq/issue/ENT-488/speed-up-integration-ci-by-skipping-gnome-keyring-install\",\"gitBranchName\":\"alex/ent-488-speed-up-integration-ci-by-skipping-gnome-keyring-install\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-04-17T02:27:52.211Z\",\"updatedAt\":\"2026-04-17T03:38:22.074Z\",\"archivedAt\":null,\"completedAt\":\"2026-04-17T03:38:22.055Z\",\"startedAt\":\"2026-04-17T02:28:10.600Z\",\"canceledAt\":null,\"dueDate\":null,\"slaStartedAt\":null,\"slaMediumRiskAt\":null,\"slaHighRiskAt\":null,\"slaBreachesAt\":null,\"slaType\":\"all\",\"status\":\"Done\",\"statusType\":\"completed\",\"labels\":[\"hygiene\",\"Improvement\"],\"attachments\":[{\"id\":\"a85006d3-b58f-4837-9025-3d9a7f9aa87c\",\"title\":\"ENT-488: skip gnome-keyring install in integration CI\",\"subtitle\":null,\"url\":\"https://github.com/entirehq/entiredb/pull/846\"}],\"documents\":[],\"createdBy\":\"Alex Ong\",\"createdById\":\"45a00cf6-3a37-45ab-a508-d9da7f9d514c\",\"assignee\":\"Alex Ong\",\"assigneeId\":\"45a00cf6-3a37-45ab-a508-d9da7f9d514c\",\"team\":\"Entire\",\"teamId\":\"832db0be-d9d8-45dc-9774-7f35babe62c0\",\"relations\":{\"blocks\":[],\"blockedBy\":[],\"relatedTo\":[],\"duplicateOf\":null}}"}],"isError":false}}}}
{"timestamp":"2026-05-08T11:03:12.640Z","type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"function_call_output","call_id":"call_kAL0B09We6ngl3sm1Xk9Ohmy","output":"Wall time: 0.9343 seconds\nOutput:\n[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"{\\\"id\\\":\\\"ENT-488\\\",\\\"title\\\":\\\"Speed up integration CI by skipping gnome-keyring install\\\",\\\"description\\\":\\\"## Context\\\\n\\\\nThe `integration` job in `.github/workflows/ci-integration.yml` currently spends \\\\\\\\~4 minutes on `apt-get update && apt-get install -y gnome-keyring dbus-x11` and related daemon setup. That's roughly half of the \\\\\\\\~9m30s job.\\\\n\\\\nTiming from run 24544052559 (temp/2 PR #843):\\\\n\\\\n| Phase | Duration |\\\\n| -- | -- |\\\\n| Setup Keyring and Identity | 4m25s |\\\\n| Run integration tests | 4m36s |\\\\n| Everything else | \\\\\\\\~30s |\\\\n\\\\nWithin the test step, `go: downloading` + compile is \\\\\\\\~10s — deps are not the problem.\\\\n\\\\n## Why the keyring is there\\\\n\\\\nThe integration tests exercise the CLI auth flow, which stores OAuth tokens via the `tokenstore` package. Its default backend delegates to the OS keyring via `github.com/zalando/go-keyring`, which on Linux talks to the Secret Service over dbus — hence the gnome-keyring install.\\\\n\\\\nOn user workstations the CLI does use the OS keyring (macOS Keychain / Linux Secret Service / Windows Credential Manager). Server nodes don't import `tokenstore` at all, so this is purely a CLI + CI concern.\\\\n\\\\n## The fix already exists\\\\n\\\\nPR #457 (`89230ae1`) added a file-backed `tokenstore` backend **explicitly for CI environments without a system keyring**, gated by `ENTIRE_TOKEN_STORE=file`. `.github/workflows/perf-nightly.yml` uses it. `ci-integration.yml` was never updated.\\\\n\\\\nProposed change: set `ENTIRE_TOKEN_STORE: file` in the integration job's `env:` block and delete the gnome-keyring install step. Expected saving: \\\\\\\\~4 minutes per run.\\\\n\\\\n## Follow-ups (separate tickets)\\\\n\\\\n* `entireio/cli` also installs gnome-keyring in its CI (Stefan copied the pattern from entiredb in Mar 2026). Could adopt the same file-backed approach there.\\\\n* `entire.io/test` package runs as a single 2m42s serial block — splitting into subpackages or using `t.Parallel()` would shave further time.\\\\n* `test:simulation` runs sequentially after integration tests in the same shell task; could be a parallel GHA job.\\\",\\\"priority\\\":{\\\"value\\\":3,\\\"name\\\":\\\"Medium\\\"},\\\"url\\\":\\\"https://linear.app/entirehq/issue/ENT-488/speed-up-integration-ci-by-skipping-gnome-keyring-install\\\",\\\"gitBranchName\\\":\\\"alex/ent-488-speed-up-integration-ci-by-skipping-gnome-keyring-install\\\",\\\"createdAt\\\":\\\"2026-04-17T02:27:52.211Z\\\",\\\"updatedAt\\\":\\\"2026-04-17T03:38:22.074Z\\\",\\\"archivedAt\\\":null,\\\"completedAt\\\":\\\"2026-04-17T03:38:22.055Z\\\",\\\"startedAt\\\":\\\"2026-04-17T02:28:10.600Z\\\",\\\"canceledAt\\\":null,\\\"dueDate\\\":null,\\\"slaStartedAt\\\":null,\\\"slaMediumRiskAt\\\":null,\\\"slaHighRiskAt\\\":null,\\\"slaBreachesAt\\\":null,\\\"slaType\\\":\\\"all\\\",\\\"status\\\":\\\"Done\\\",\\\"statusType\\\":\\\"completed\\\",\\\"labels\\\":[\\\"hygiene\\\",\\\"Improvement\\\"],\\\"attachments\\\":[{\\\"id\\\":\\\"a85006d3-b58f-4837-9025-3d9a7f9aa87c\\\",\\\"title\\\":\\\"ENT-488: skip gnome-keyring install in integration CI\\\",\\\"subtitle\\\":null,\\\"url\\\":\\\"https://github.com/entirehq/entiredb/pull/846\\\"}],\\\"documents\\\":[],\\\"createdBy\\\":\\\"Alex Ong\\\",\\\"createdById\\\":\\\"45a00cf6-3a37-45ab-a508-d9da7f9d514c\\\",\\\"assignee\\\":\\\"Alex Ong\\\",\\\"assigneeId\\\":\\\"45a00cf6-3a37-45ab-a508-d9da7f9d514c\\\",\\\"team\\\":\\\"Entire\\\",\\\"teamId\\\":\\\"832db0be-d9d8-45dc-9774-7f35babe62c0\\\",\\\"relations\\\":{\\\"blocks\\\":[],\\\"blockedBy\\\":[],\\\"relatedTo\\\":[],\\\"duplicateOf\\\":null}}\"}]"}}
